{
  "_note": "Written by the Settings modal (live pill -> Settings) and read by tools/scalper.py --registered and tools/event_alert.py on every run. Safe to hand-edit; the UI rewrites the whole file, so a comment added here will not survive a save -- put explanations in the per-cell `note` field, which does. A cell is TRADEABLE only if its median sub-era and its total R/yr agree in sign; only tradeable cells are messaged, the rest are journalled. The retired Donchian forward test lives in configs/retired/donchian_forward_test.json.",
  "news": {
    "enabled": true,
    "lead_minutes": 10,
    "impact": "low",
    "fetch_minutes": 360
  },
  "scalper": {
    "registered": "2026-09-14",
    "rule": "rayo_scalper break mode: swing 20, EMA 20/50, stop 5 ATR, entry 0.10 ATR beyond the swing, exit TP1 (0.9R), expire 12 bars, SESSION OFF (24h) -- the gate measured +42% on total R/yr and is switched off by request; pass --session 7-21 to compare against pre-2026-09-10 numbers.",
    "journal": "data/scalper_journal.jsonl",
    "scored_with": "python tools/score_scalper.py -- hourly via the \"DiaNurFx-Score-Scalper\" task. It resolves each journalled ticket on 1m bars FROM THE BRIDGE (true UTC, the clock the journal is in -- not the broker-time archive), reusing tools/scalper.py resolve() so a live number and a registered number cannot disagree for reasons nobody can find. Tickets are grouped by stop_atr so the 4.0 and 5.0 eras are never pooled. tools/score_external.py grades hand-logged THIRD-PARTY signals and is not this.",
    "why_separate": "not a sim.Strategy -- pending orders that fill intrabar and a three-rung TP ladder, neither of which the engine models -- so it is scored by tools/scalper.py, not polled through the bridge /signal",
